Opaque focus wide ramp (dcsvr_two_layers_alpha=3, after 0025; native/quadviews/dcsvr_twolayer_ps.hlsl): 0025's thin rim did
not remove the line: the verification flights of 2026-11-22 showed a thin warm line along all four edges of the focus
rectangle in both eyes in the Pimax screen mirror, none in the undistorted mirror. Across every edge green is unchanged,
red rises by 35 % and blue falls by 41 % of the background (sky 138/178/222 -> 193/178/131, a dark edge 18/30/52 ->
25/30/32), red's band one mirror pixel outside blue's. That is the runtime's distortion sampling each colour channel at
its own place (chromatic aberration correction) and blending with one alpha, green's: shown_c = F_c(x_c) a(x_c) +
D_c(x_c) (1 - a(x_G)), so any alpha that changes within a few texels gives red and blue D (a(x_c) - a(x_G)) too much or
too little. The same formula gives 0024's blue 0 / red 255 (hard edge) and 0025's line (a ramp of 15 texels against an
offset of about 5). The focus pass now stores as alpha the composition's own fade at the pixel's own place, never
steeper than the band of edge blend 0.2 (the outer 0.4 of the radius), and the colour for that alpha as before
(P + (C - P) / a), so the residual is a few codes spread over the band. Here: the flag comment and the log line.
